<title>USA: US Industries issues notes, gets credit.</title>
<headline>US Industries issues notes, gets credit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Industries Inc said it issued a $125 million offering of senior notes and entered into a $750 million unsecured revolving credit facility.</p>
<p>The notes yield 7 1/4 percent and are due December 1, 2006, the company said.</p>
<p>They were priced December 6 to yield 7.358 percent, according to the company, which will use the notes' proceeds to prepay existing term loans, it said.</p>
<p>The company also said it will prepay the rest of its existing credit facility at reduced borrowing rates, based on its current credit rating.</p>
</text>
